{"result":"{
  "id": "19311",
  "key": "SFCC-816",
  "summary": "Cart Summary Component UI – PWA Kit",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Order Summary*\n\n# Given a Shopper views the cart, when the cart summary component renders, then the order summary displays the following elements: Total Items count, Shipping method and cost, Subtotal, Tax amount, and Grand Total — all right-aligned with their corresponding labels left-aligned.\n# Given an error condition exists in the cart, when the cart summary component renders, then an error message is displayed in red above the Checkout CTA within the order summary.\n\n*Button Group*\n\n# Given the cart contains one or more items, when the cart summary component renders, then the button group displays in the following order: Checkout CTA, Apple Pay Express, Google Pay Express\n\n*Duties and Taxes*\n\n# Given the duties and taxes text is configured to display for a storefront, when the cart summary component renders, then a text line is displayed reading \"Duties and taxes are included in the price displayed.\"\n# Given the duties and taxes text is not configured for a storefront, when the cart summary component renders, then the duties and taxes text line is not shown and the surrounding layout is unaffected.\n\n*Promotion Code Accordion*\n\n# Given a Shopper views the cart summary, when the component renders, then the promotion code section displays as a collapsed accordion labelled ADD PROMOTION CODE with a chevron icon.\n# Given a Shopper clicks the ADD PROMOTION CODE accordion, when it expands, then a text input field and an Apply button are revealed.\n# Given a Shopper has entered text into the promotion code input field, when text is present, then a clear/X icon is displayed within the input field.\n## All promotion code entry, validation, success and error states are covered in [SFCC-191]\n\n*Recommended for You*\n\n# Given a Shopper views the cart summary, when the component renders, then the Recommended for You carousel is displayed below the promotion code accordion. \n## Full Recommendation Cart UI Component is covered here - see [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-815|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-815|smart-link]  \n\n*Responsive*\n\n# Given a Shopper views the cart on any device, when the cart summary component renders, then it displays correctly across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications.\n\n*Accessibility:*\n\n# Given the order summary renders within the cart summary component, when read by a screen reader, then all values (Total Items, Shipping, Subtotal, Tax, Grand Total) are announced in a logical top-to-bottom reading order with their corresponding labels.\n# Given an error message renders within the order summary (e.g. OOS, limited stock, max quantity), when it appears, then it is announced immediately via an ARIA live region (role=\"alert\") so the Shopper is informed without having to navigate to it.\n# Given the Checkout CTA renders within the cart summary component, when read by a screen reader, then it is announced as a button with a descriptive label (e.g. \"Checkout\").\n# Given the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay Express, and Google Pay Express buttons are disabled in the back end due to a cart error, when read by a screen reader, then each button is announced as disabled so the Shopper understands the actions are not currently available.\n# Given the Apple Pay and Google Pay Express buttons render within the cart summary component, when read by a screen reader, then each button is announced with a descriptive label (e.g. \"Pay with Apple Pay\", \"Pay with Google Pay\").\n# Given the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay Express, and Google Pay Express buttons render within the cart summary component, when a Shopper navigates via keyboard, then each button is focusable and activatable via the Enter key in a logical top-to-bottom tab order.\n# Given the duties and taxes text line renders within the cart summary component, when read by a screen reader, then it is announced as static text in a logical reading order between the button group and the promotion code accordion.\n# Given the promotion code accordion renders within the cart summary component, when navigated via keyboard or read by a screen reader, then the accordion toggle is focusable, activatable via the Enter key, and its expanded/collapsed state is announced correctly via aria-expanded.\n# Given the promotion code input field renders within the expanded accordion, when read by a screen reader, then the input field has a descriptive label and the clear/X icon is announced as a button with an accessible label (e.g. \"Clear promotion code\").\n# Given the Recommended for You carousel renders within the cart summary component, when navigated via keyboard, then carousel items are focusable and navigable in a logical order — see SFCC-118 for full carousel accessibility requirements.\n# Given a Shopper navigates the cart summary component via keyboard, when they tab through it, then focus moves in a logical top-to-bottom order: order summary → Checkout CTA → Apple Pay → Google Pay → duties and taxes text → promotion code accordion → Recommended for You carousel.\n# Given any text or interactive element renders within the cart summary component, when checked against WCAG 2.1 AA standards, then all text meets a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 and all interactive elements meet a minimum contrast ratio of 3:1."
  }
}"}
